# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  DON'T PANIC. 🐬
#
#  You do not need any of this to run the valuation walkthrough.
#
#      uv sync
#      uv run jupyter lab
#
#  gets you the whole notebook - loading a county roll, building the
#  gradient boosting model, the ratio statistics, SHAP - with no keys,
#  no accounts and no internet beyond installing the packages.
#
#  Everything below is for ONE optional feature: the chat assistant at
#  the very end of the Streamlit app, which lets you ask questions about
#  your roll in plain English.
#
#  ── To use it ────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
#      cp .env.example .env          (macOS / Linux)
#      copy .env.example .env        (Windows cmd)
#      Copy-Item .env.example .env   (PowerShell)
#
#  Then fill in the one value you need and save.
#
#  🔒 .env is git-ignored. NEVER commit it. This file (.env.example) IS
#     committed on purpose - it names the variables and holds no values.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────


# ── The hosted chat assistant ────────────────────────────────
#
# This is the only variable most people need.
#
# Get a key at: https://console.anthropic.com
#
# You can also leave this blank and paste a key straight into the box in
# the app's chat section - handy on a shared machine where you would
# rather not leave a key in a file. The app never prints your key.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=""

# Which model answers your questions. The app's dropdown lets you switch
# without editing this file; this just sets where it starts.
#
#   claude-haiku-5-5    fast and cheap - the default
#   claude-sonnet-5-5   more capable
#   claude-opus-5-5     most capable
#
# 📌 Why Haiku by default: most questions an assessor asks of a roll are
# straightforward - a count, a median, a breakdown by neighbourhood, a
# histogram - and Haiku answers those perfectly well for a fraction of the
# cost. An office trying this out should not meet the bill before it finds
# out whether the tool is useful.
#
# ⚠️ Switch up for a question worth more thought. The assistant writes SQL
# against your roll, and a wrong query becomes a confident wrong answer
# about somebody's property. If an answer looks off, ask Sonnet or Opus the
# same question before believing either of them.
#
# Put any model id here, even one not in the list. It gets its own entry in
# the dropdown so you can see what you are using.
ANTHROPIC_MODEL="claude-haiku-5-5"


# ── The optional login screen ────────────────────────────────
#
# Leave BOTH of these unset - the default - and the app opens straight to
# the data, which is almost certainly what you want.
#
# Set BOTH and the app asks for them before showing anything.
#
# ⚠️ Be clear about what this is: a courtesy screen for a shared demo
# laptop, NOT security. The app reads public taxroll data and serves it
# on localhost. Do not put anything behind it that would matter if seen.
#HGMA_APP_USER=""
#HGMA_APP_PASSWORD=""


# ── Running a model on your own machine instead ──────────────
#
# For the local variant of the chat assistant, where no data leaves the
# building. In a lot of assessor's offices that is the only version IT
# will approve, which is exactly why it exists.
#
# Needs the optional extra, which is a ~3 GB download:
#
#      uv sync --extra slm
#
# ⚠️ And a warning that will bite you: a plain `uv sync` afterwards
# PRUNES that extra back out again, silently. Re-run it with
# `--extra slm` and it is quick, because the wheels are cached.
LOCAL_MODEL="Qwen/Qwen3.5-4B"

# Only needed to DOWNLOAD the local model the first time. A free "Read"
# token is all you need: https://huggingface.co/settings/tokens
#HF_TOKEN=""

# Set both to 1 once the model is cached to force fully offline mode.
# Useful before a presentation: guarantees no network call can hang it.
HF_HUB_OFFLINE=0
TRANSFORMERS_OFFLINE=0
